<.error_page
  context="Error"
  status={500}
  subtitle="Internal server error — your request was not applied."
>
  <:title>
    Something went wrong on our side
  </:title>
  <p class="text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">
    The server hit an unexpected error while handling this request. Nothing you did caused it, and these problems are usually temporary — retrying in a moment often works.
  </p>
  <%= case assigns[:conn] do %>
    <% %{request_path: request_path} -> %>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <.link href={request_path} class="btn btn-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-arrow-path" class="size-4" /> Try again
        </.link>
        <.link href={~p"/"} class="link link-primary text-sm font-semibold">Back to home →</.link>
      </div>
    <% _ -> %>
  <% end %>
  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
    If it keeps happening, tell us via the
    <.link href={~p"/contact"} class="link link-primary">contact page</.link>
    — the address you were visiting and the approximate time help us find it. If you believe you've found a security vulnerability, use the process in our
    <.link href={~p"/security-policy"} class="link link-primary">security policy</.link>
    instead.
  </p>
</.error_page>
